      "instructions": [
        "Preheat oven to 400°F (200°C). Line a baking sheet with parchment paper.",
        "Rinse quinoa under cold water. In a small saucepan, combine quinoa with 1.5 cups vegetable broth or water. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat to low, cover, and simmer for 15 minutes, or until all liquid is absorbed. Fluff with a fork.",
        "Trim the woody ends off the asparagus. Toss asparagus with 1 tablespoon olive oil, salt, and pepper on the prepared baking sheet.",
        "Pat salmon fillets dry with a paper towel. Place them on the same baking sheet alongside the asparagus. Drizzle salmon with remaining 0.5 tablespoon olive oil, sprinkle with garlic powder, dried dill (if using), salt, and pepper. Top each fillet with a lemon slice.",
        "Roast for 12-15 minutes, or until salmon is cooked through and flakes easily with a fork, and asparagus is tender-crisp.",
        "Serve salmon and asparagus immediately with a side of fluffy quinoa. Squeeze fresh lemon juice over the salmon if desired."
      ],
